{
  "body_human_readable": "**\"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Hits Theaters with a $45-50 Million Budget, Grosses Over $100 Million Worldwide**\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction novel, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to achieve a worldwide box office gross of over $100 million.\n\nThe film, directed by Garth Jennings, was released in the United Kingdom on April 28, 2005, and a day later in North America. It opened in first place in the North American box office, earning $21.1 million in its opening weekend. The total worldwide gross for the movie is reported as $104.5 million, with another source stating it at $102.7 million.\n\n\"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" starred Martin Freeman as the bewildered human Arthur Dent, alongside Sam Rockwell, Mos Def, Zooey Deschanel, and Bill Nighy. The screenplay was co-written by Adams and Karey Kirkpatrick, and the film is dedicated to Adams, who passed away in 2001 before production began.",
